  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Split Flap\n\nAn airport-style departure board where each word flips onto a row of flap tiles, letter by letter, through a list of places before it lands on a final word; a status line changes from searching to confirmed.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A list of options (cities, offers, names) that cycles on a physical board and lands on a final word.\n- A mechanical feel for a destination, price or status reveal.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A caption that should flip letters in time with speech: use caption-split-flap.\n- Very long words: each letter is a tile.\n\nVariables:\n- words (string): Words, default \"PARIS, LONDON, TOKYO, NEW YORK, SYDNEY, BERLIN, WELCOME\"\n- label (string): Label, default \"DESTINATION\"\n- status_busy (string): Status while flipping, default \"SEARCHING...\"\n- status_done (string): Status at the end, default \"CONFIRMED\"\n- font_size (number, 16-160): Font size, default 48\n- color (color): Letter color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- accent (color): Final color, default \"#2563eb\"\n- tile (color): Tile color, default \"#262626\"\n- success (color): Status dot, default \"#2563eb\"\n- background (color): Background, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Split Flap\n\n  An airport-style departure board where each word flips onto a row of flap tiles, letter by letter, through a list of places before it lands on a final word; a status line changes from searching to confirmed.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerSplitFlap.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-split-flap\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"words\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Words\", \"description\": \"Words in order, separated by commas (up to 10). The last one is where it settles.\", \"default\": \"PARIS, LONDON, TOKYO, NEW YORK, SYDNEY, BERLIN, WELCOME\"},\n    {\"id\": \"label\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Label\", \"description\": \"Small caps line above the board.\", \"default\": \"DESTINATION\"},\n    {\"id\": \"status_busy\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Status while flipping\", \"description\": \"Text under the board before the last word.\", \"default\": \"SEARCHING...\"},\n    {\"id\": \"status_done\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Status at the end\", \"description\": \"Text under the board once the last word is shown.\", \"default\": \"CONFIRMED\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the letters in pixels. The board shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 48, \"min\": 16, \"max\": 160, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Letter color\", \"description\": \"Color of the letters.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Final color\", \"description\": \"Color of the last word.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"tile\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Tile color\", \"description\": \"Color of each flap tile.\", \"default\": \"#262626\"},\n    {\"id\": \"success\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Status dot\", \"description\": \"Color of the status dot at the end.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Split Flap</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wsf-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: var(--c, #fafafa); }\n        .wsf-g { text-align: center; line-height: 1; }\n        .wsf-lead { font-size: 0.292em; color: #a3a3a3; letter-spacing: 0.286em; margin-bottom: 1.43em; white-space: pre; }\n        .wsf-board { display: inline-flex; gap: 0.167em; background: #171717; padding: 0.417em 0.625em; border-radius: 0.167em; }\n        .wsf-tile { position: relative; width: 1.04em; height: 1.458em; background: var(--tl, #262626); border-radius: 0.083em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: inset 0 0.02em 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.06); }\n        .wsf-tile::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 50%; height: 0.04em; background: #171717; transform: translateY(-50%); z-index: 1; }\n        .wsf-tile span { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; }\n        .wsf-status { margin-top: 1.9em; font-size: 0.333em; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.6em; }\n        .wsf-dot { width: 0.5em; height: 0.5em; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--ok, #2563eb); display: none; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-split-flap\" data-duration=\"4\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wsf-clip\" class=\"wsf-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wsf-g\" class=\"wsf-g\">\n            <div id=\"wsf-lead\" class=\"wsf-lead\"></div>\n            <div id=\"wsf-board\" class=\"wsf-board\"></div>\n            <div class=\"wsf-status\"><span id=\"wsf-dot\" class=\"wsf-dot\"></span><span id=\"wsf-st\"></span></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-split-flap\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#0a0a0a\");\n            \n            var words = list(vars.words, [\"PARIS\", \"LONDON\", \"TOKYO\", \"NEW YORK\", \"SYDNEY\", \"BERLIN\", \"WELCOME\"], 10);\n            var fi = words.length - 1;\n            var maxLen = Math.max.apply(null, words.map(function (w) { return Array.from(w).length; }));\n            var g = el(\"wsf-g\"), lead = el(\"wsf-lead\"), board = el(\"wsf-board\"), dot = el(\"wsf-dot\"), st = el(\"wsf-st\");\n            var color = str(vars.color, \"#fafafa\"), accent = str(vars.accent, \"#2563eb\"), ok = str(vars.success, \"#2563eb\");\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--c\", color);\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--tl\", str(vars.tile, \"#262626\"));\n            root.style.setProperty(\"--ok\", ok);\n            lead.textContent = txt(vars.label, \"DESTINATION\");\n            lead.style.display = lead.textContent ? \"\" : \"none\";\n            var busy = txt(vars.status_busy, \"SEARCHING...\"), done = txt(vars.status_done, \"CONFIRMED\");\n            var tiles = [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < maxLen; i++) {\n              var t = document.createElement(\"div\");\n              t.className = \"wsf-tile\";\n              var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              t.appendChild(s);\n              board.appendChild(t);\n              tiles.push(s);\n            }\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 48, 16, 160);\n            function fit() { fitG(g, base, null, 0.9, 0.8); }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n\n            // remocn-scenes: 90 frames shared between the words; after the first frames of a word a spring\n            // (damping 20, stiffness 400) flips its tiles from edge-on, one frame apart left to right.\n            function draw(f) {\n              var D = 90, wd = D / words.length;\n              var wi = Math.min(Math.floor(f / wd), fi);\n              var final = wi === fi;\n              var wp = final ? clamp01((f - fi * wd) / wd) : (f % wd) / wd;\n              var chars = Array.from(words[wi]);\n              var fr = Math.floor(wp * 15);\n              tiles.forEach(function (s, i) {\n                setText(s, chars[i] === undefined ? \" \" : chars[i]);\n                s.style.color = final ? accent : color;\n                var p = spring(fr - i, { damping: 20, stiffness: 400 });\n                s.style.transform = \"rotateX(\" + ((1 - Math.min(1, p)) * 90) + \"deg)\";\n              });\n              setText(st, final ? done : busy);\n              st.parentNode.style.color = final ? color : \"#a3a3a3\";\n              dot.style.display = final ? \"block\" : \"none\";\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
